{
 "title": "Stereoid",
 "children": [
  {
   "title": "Overview",
   "lines": [
    "A stereo widener with",
    "four engines.",
    "",
    "Comb, Haas and",
    "Disperse CREATE width:",
    "they do the most to",
    "mono or centred",
    "sounds.",
    "",
    "M/S turns up the",
    "width a stereo source",
    "already has.",
    "",
    "WIDE 0 is a true",
    "bypass in every",
    "engine."
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Engines",
   "children": [
    {
     "title": "Comb",
     "lines": [
      "Adds a delayed copy",
      "of the mid to one",
      "side and takes it",
      "from the other.",
      "",
      "No lean, and the mono",
      "sum is exactly the",
      "input. The sign of",
      "WIDE mirrors the comb."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Haas",
     "lines": [
      "Delays one side. The",
      "image leans toward",
      "the side that arrives",
      "first: that is the",
      "character.",
      "",
      "+ delays the right,",
      "- the left. LATE sets",
      "the delayed side's",
      "level."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Disperse",
     "lines": [
      "An all-pass and comb",
      "widener, modelled from",
      "measurement.",
      "",
      "Each channel widens",
      "from itself, so a",
      "hard-panned sound",
      "stays on its side.",
      "",
      "Mono sum exact for a",
      "mono input."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "M/S",
     "lines": [
      "Scales the side the",
      "input already has.",
      "",
      "-100 is mono, 0 is",
      "unchanged, +100",
      "doubles the side.",
      "",
      "Does nothing to a",
      "mono source. The mid",
      "never changes."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Controls",
   "children": [
    {
     "title": "Wide",
     "lines": [
      "-100 to +100.",
      "",
      "How wide. 0 is a true",
      "bypass. The sign picks",
      "the side or mirrors",
      "the comb. In M/S it is",
      "the side's level."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Wide Freq",
     "lines": [
      "Nothing below it is",
      "widened, so the low",
      "end stays where it",
      "was.",
      "",
      "20 Hz is full band."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Time",
     "lines": [
      "The delay, 0 to 12 ms.",
      "",
      "0 is Auto: each",
      "engine's own. In Haas,",
      "setting it makes WIDE",
      "the delayed side's",
      "mix.",
      "",
      "Not in M/S."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Trim",
     "lines": [
      "Output level, -12 to",
      "0 dB, by hand."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Comp",
     "lines": [
      "A trim that follows",
      "the width.",
      "",
      "Loud holds loudness",
      "(up to -3 dB).",
      "Peak holds the worst",
      "case peak (up to",
      "-6 dB).",
      "",
      "Both lower the mono",
      "sum; Off keeps it",
      "exact."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "High Cut",
     "lines": [
      "Nothing above it is",
      "widened.",
      "",
      "20 kHz is off."
     ]
    },
    {
     "title": "Late Level",
     "lines": [
      "Haas only. The delayed",
      "side's level, +/-12 dB.",
      "",
      "Up counters the lean,",
      "down deepens it."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Headroom",
   "lines": [
    "A widener adds to",
    "each channel: at full",
    "width one can reach",
    "twice the input.",
    "Nothing here limits",
    "it.",
    "",
    "Use Trim or Comp if",
    "it clips."
   ]
  }
 ]
}
